# Cursor Rules — Gillespie Fire Check App

You are helping build a client-side web app for Gillespie Fire Department monthly apparatus and SCBA checklists.

## Context
- Pure HTML/CSS/JS. No build step required.
- Data lives in `data.js`. UI logic in `app.js`. Styles in `styles.css`.
- Goal: reliable offline-capable checklist tool that firefighters can use on tablets/phones, print or export PDF, and keep drafts in localStorage.

## Current priorities (see PROJECT_STATUS.md for details)
1. Sync HTML button IDs with the handlers in `app.js` (`export-pdf-btn` vs `export-btn`, wire `save-btn`).
2. Implement localStorage draft save/load (currently missing entirely).
3. Add the jsPDF CDN script so PDF export works.
4. Clean up the completed-by / date / signature section so there is only one set of fields.
5. Replace the “FD” logo placeholder with the real department logo when available.

## Style preferences
- Keep the existing dark theme (black/red/yellow accents).
- Prefer clear, readable code over clever one-liners.
- Mobile-first responsive layout.
- Do not introduce a framework or build system unless explicitly asked.

## When making changes
- Preserve the existing checklist data structure in `data.js`.
- Test both normal apparatus units and the special SCBA multi-pack flow.
- Keep print styles working.
- Update PROJECT_STATUS.md if you resolve a listed issue.
